But it's not about the movement.  It's about training that spell
school.  Here, I'll dash off a little commentary on exercising
spell schools -

Use level 1 spells to do it because they cost fewer
power points and have higher success rates.  A spell
school is trained with a successfull cast so failed
attempts of higher level spells aren't the way to
move up towards Expert in any one school.  Even
though it takes more attempts with the lower class
spells the lower failure rates and simpler natures of
the spells make it worth doing.

Attack school - Force bolt is only level 1 spell so
casting it again and again is the way to advance
Attack.  As a wizard it's a starting spell so it can
be used regularly in combat before you get Magic
Missile.

Healing school - Regular healing is the only level 1
spell so casting it regularly while in combat is the
way to advance Healing.

Divination - Detect monsters and light are the level
1 spells in this class.  Feel free to gradually light
up entire levels as a way to advance this class.  Also
use detect monsters regularly until offered an advance.

Enchantment - Sleep is the only level 1 spell and it
is usefull in combat.  Use it again and again until
offered an advance.  Sleep spells work well while altar
camping - Zap a victim monster with sleep, kill it using
whatever means with the first hit free, sacrafice it
at the altar.

Clerical - Protection is the only level 1 spell in
this class.  But create monster is a level 2 spell.
For classes that don't get hunger-free casting protection
gives temporary AC boost.  For classes that do get
hunger-free casting create monster means excellent altar
camping.

Escape - Jumping is the only level 1 spell.  Once the
jump spell is known cast it again and again until offered
advance in escape.  For training purposes jumping is not
a faster travel method but simply a school homework
lesson.  Move from level to level jumping until power
goes down to half way point then walk or teleport the
rest of the way, and viola you'll be better at the more
important but higher level spells in this school.

Matter - Knock is the only level 1 spell in this school
so open and close doors with it to be able to better use
the more powerfull spells in the Matter school.

Consider from the spoilers: "Castings to a total of 20 are
needed to achieve basic level, 80 to become skilled, and
180 to become expert, with each spell cast contributing a
number equal to its level to this total. These are
cumulative from the beginning of the game ..."  So it may
take 180 jumps to reach Expert in Escape but those jumps
can be practiced while moving among levels and so on for
all of the other schools you are interested in.

